    {
      "id": "2120798842451058773",
      "text": "RT @NarutoNolimits: Why Elon Musk believes we could colonize the entire galaxy in a million years\n\nTo Elon Musk, it's not even a hard quest…",
      "created_at": "Thu Nov 12 08:40:21 +0000 2026",
      "lang": "en",
      "media": [],
      "retweet": {
        "id": "2120625963495277052",
        "text": "Why Elon Musk believes we could colonize the entire galaxy in a million years\n\nTo Elon Musk, it's not even a hard question.\n\nA million years is enough to spread across the whole galaxy.\n\nSo where is everyone?\n\nNobody seems to have done it.\n\nSomething stops civilizations before they get out there. That's the great filter.\n\nAnd it's why he thinks about Mars with one specific test.\n\nElon: \"Do we have enough resources on Mars such that if the spaceships from Earth stopped coming, you can survive?\"\n\nJoe Rogan compared it to a long sea voyage where the only thing you're missing is vitamin C.\n\nAnd the ships could stop for reasons that aren't dramatic at all.\n\nCivilization on Earth could end with a bang or a whimper.\n\nA Mars that can survive on its own is how he thinks we get past the filter. https://t.co/GMPF5sI4wG",
